  "method": "Subagents driving the atelier MCP server, one agent per task, each loading the atelier-sprite skill and working only through atelier's tools — the Anthropic models via Claude Code, kimi-k3 via Kimi Code. Every model draws the same ten tasks from identical frozen briefs (benchmarks/tasks/*.txt). Stats: Claude Code runs report the client's own tool_uses and subagent tokens plus each agent's self-reported doc_look count; the kimi-k3 runs report each agent's self-reported tool-call and doc_look tally (Kimi Code exposes no per-agent token usage, so its tokens are null). Durations are omitted: agents ran concurrently, so wall-clock is queueing, not work.",
